title: Add storage invariant checks to pallet-psm try_state

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Adds `do_try_state` to `pallet-psm`, wired to the `try_state` hook under the
      `try-runtime` feature. Sixteen checks cover the multi-instance storage layout:
      decimal snapshots against live metadata, reserve coverage of tracked debt,
      internal issuance against instance debt, orphaned rows without a parent PSM,
      and debt tracked for non-approved pairs.

      Four checks are advisory and log a warning rather than returning an error,
      since governance can legitimately produce those states: per-asset debt over
      its ceiling, instance debt over `max_debt`, a funded reserve with zero ceiling
      weight and zero debt, and fee or weight rows set before their external asset
      is approved.

      Each check has a corresponding unit test that corrupts exactly one storage
      item and asserts the specific failure, or asserts `Ok` for advisory checks.

crates:
  - name: pallet-psm
    bump: minor
